From: integration
Subject: --from's own tests gain the memory field --memory added to Command

feat/from-ref adds `from` to Command::Select and Command::Workspace and
constructs both in its tests. feat/memory-cap adds `memory` to the same two
variants. Each is complete on its own branch; merged, from-ref's test
initializers name every field but the one the other topic added, and a struct
initializer has to name them all.

Neither branch can carry this. from-ref cannot name a field that does not exist
on upstream, and memory-cap cannot patch tests it has never seen. It is also
not a conflict, so rerere never sees it: the two topics touch different lines
of the same file and git merges them cleanly into something that does not
compile.

Remove this when either topic lands upstream and the other is rebased onto it.
